  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-05-28T07:35:13.997Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "- Make SDK set near clipping plane to 0.01 when a new Camera is created. \n- Create a new camera with near clipping plane set 0.01 during world upload if no scene reference camera is defined.\n- Display a warning in the build panel if the near clipping plane is set bigger than 0.01 or no scene Reference Camera is set.\nReasoning: \nThis would be a solution to a problem that's been bothering me for quite a while: Worlds where your avatar or other people start to disappear/cut open before they are even close to you. Imagine a hologram that starts to disappear when you get too close to it. This has been a major immersion breaker in affected worlds.\nFor this to be fixed atm, every world author has to known about the problem and then change the world parameters.\nThe current default near clipping plane defined by Unity is 0.03 (3 cm). This doesn't seem like much distance but when you consider this scales up when using a smaller Avatar it's quite noticeable. Most worlds would experience no downside to having set the value to 0.01 (1 cm). If there are issues (mostly giant worlds), the creator can just change this value after the fact.\nThe unity default of 0.03 seems to exist with traditional non-VR games in mind. So not for games where you have full freedom of movement.",
